# The code tool's engine, pinned: the one place its build reads what it builds from (build.sh sources this; a
# change here is a change of engine, its own commit with the measures re-run).
#
# TAG          the original QuickJS's release (Fabrice Bellard's, bellard.org/quickjs): the date naming its archive
# SOURCE       the sha256 of quickjs-TAG.tar.xz — fetch checks it, and build again before use
# IMAGE        wasi-sdk's image by digest (wasi-sdk 25, clang 19.1.5): never a moving tag
# MODULE       the sha256 of the built quickjs.wasm (the stripped one, target/quickjs/quickjs.wasm): the build is
#              byte-identical from these three, so build says where its output differs, and the engine's tests
#              refuse any other module under TARAE_EXPECT_ENGINE=1 (:preflight-full's engine step). The probe
#              (out/quickjs-probe.wasm) has none: it is the tests' alone, never shipped, and made by the same build
#              from the same glue.c — the command that makes the pinned module makes it too
#
# The archive comes from one host, bellard.org/quickjs/quickjs-TAG.tar.xz, with no mirror. Any copy with SOURCE's
# sha256 serves as well (main's .sb/quickjs-bellard-2026-06-04/ keeps one): put at target/quickjs/, build checks it.
#
# At a re-pin, re-read what tarae says of the engine (src/codetool.rs), each against the new build:
# - MODULE, the new build's sha256 (build prints it, and says it differs from the old one); the engine's tests run
#   in :preflight-full's engine step, on this Mac (TARAE_EXPECT_ENGINE=1: a missing module or another fails them;
#   CI has no module, and they skip there) — run that step on the new build;
# - the figures glue.c builds in: CALLS (MAX_CALLS), PRINTED_MAX, ENGINE_HEAP (MEMORY_LIMIT, the memory
#   ending's figure; `the_engines_heap_limit_is_glues` holds it to glue.c);
# - ENGINE_OUT_OF_MEMORY, the words for the heap limit met (glue.c's OUT_OF_MEMORY, the engine's own throw's);
# - the out-of-memory guard (glue.c's `oom`). The cap is the allocator's refusal at ENGINE_HEAP, and it holds with
#   or without the guard; the guard makes the ending final and exact. What it stands on, a refused allocation
#   never retried: `codetool::tests::the_engine_never_retries_a_refused_allocation` on out/quickjs-probe.wasm,
#   every refusal of its bodies walked — it shows the ending is never early, and no refusal is swallowed; and the
#   allocator read again (`__js_malloc`/`__js_realloc`, a new caller that swallows a NULL, an out-of-memory throw
#   that isn't a refusal);
# - the stack (glue.c's STACK_LIMIT, set past `JS_NewRuntime2`'s): `deep_recursion_is_an_error_the_program_sees`;
# - FUEL_A_STEP and LIMITS.steps, measured again (`codetool::tests::measure`), and the work the steps don't see
#   (`codetool::tests::HEAVY`);
# - the fuzz hour again, the JIT against the interpreter on the new build, on each architecture whose
#   `LIMITS.jit` is true (aarch64), on a quiet machine: tarae-wasm's crate doc has the commands
#   (`examples/qjs_fuzz.rs`). Clean, G36's row in docs/threat-model.md takes the new seeds, count and the
#   engine's sha256; not clean, that architecture's `LIMITS.jit` goes false until it is. (A change to
#   tarae-wasm's `jit/` means the hour too.)
